the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt holds for *a case*.
    Merkmal 1 holds for *a case*; open textured.
    Merkmal 2 holds for *a case*; open textured.
    Merkmal 3 holds for *a case*; open textured.
    child *a number* of Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt counts for *a case*.
    Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt is decided for *a case*.
    Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt would hold for *a case*; unknown.
    Merkmal 1 is decided for *a case*; scenario element.
    Merkmal 2 is decided for *a case*; scenario element.
    Merkmal 3 is decided for *a case*; scenario element.

the knowledge base r3_6_majority_of_children includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/majority-of-children.ruml".

child 1 of Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt counts for a case if
    Merkmal 1 holds for the case.

child 2 of Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt counts for a case if
    Merkmal 2 holds for the case.

child 3 of Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt counts for a case if
    Merkmal 3 holds for the case.

% Mehr als die Hälfte der ausgewerteten Merkmale muss erfüllt sein
Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt holds for a case if
    Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt is decided for the case
    and a number M is the count of each N such that
        child a number N of Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt counts for the case
    and a number K = M * 2
    and K > 3.

Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt holds for a case if
    it is not the case that Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt is decided for the case
    and Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt would hold for the case.

Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt is decided for a case if
    Merkmal 1 is decided for the case
    and Merkmal 2 is decided for the case
    and Merkmal 3 is decided for the case.

scenario generated_1 is, as stated in "majority-of-children.ruml" at generated_1:
    % no data
    node_1 expects answers ["Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    node_2 expects answers ["Merkmal 1 holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_2 expects answers ["it is not the case that Merkmal 1 holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    node_3 expects answers ["Merkmal 2 holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_3 expects answers ["it is not the case that Merkmal 2 holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    node_4 expects answers ["Merkmal 3 holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_4 expects answers ["it is not the case that Merkmal 3 holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.

query node_1 is:
    Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt holds for case 1.

query not_node_1 is:
    it is not the case that Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt holds for case 1.

query node_2 is:
    Merkmal 1 holds for case 1.

query not_node_2 is:
    it is not the case that Merkmal 1 holds for case 1.

query node_3 is:
    Merkmal 2 holds for case 1.

query not_node_3 is:
    it is not the case that Merkmal 2 holds for case 1.

query node_4 is:
    Merkmal 3 holds for case 1.

query not_node_4 is:
    it is not the case that Merkmal 3 holds for case 1.

